        "content": "{\n  \"quantitative_comparisons\": [],\n  \"usable_content\": \"现有文献中尚未发现已完成的大规模III期随机对照试验（RCT）报告微生物组干预（如FMT、益生菌或定义明确的菌群联合体）联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗实体瘤的主要疗效结果（OS/PFS/ORR）。截至2025年底的综述明确指出，该领域目前缺乏III期确认性证据，现有证据主要依赖于I期和II期单臂试验及荟萃分析。具体而言，MIMic试验（NCT03772899）是一项针对晚期黑色素瘤患者的多中心I期单臂安全性试验，评估口服FMT联合抗PD-1疗法，报告了客观缓解率（ORR）为65%，中位无进展生存期（mPFS）为29.6个月，中位总生存期（mOS）为52.8个月，但作者强调样本量小且无对照组，结果仅为假设生成性质。另一项FMT-LUMINate试验（NCT04951583）是涉及20名未接受过治疗的晚期黑色素瘤患者的II期单臂研究，评估FMT联合双免疫检查点抑制剂（伊匹木单抗和纳武利尤单抗），报告ORR为70%，但同时也观察到65%的患者出现3级以上免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。这些早期阶段的研究虽然提供了机制见解（如响应者富集短链脂肪酸产生菌）和支持未来随机试验的理由，但并未提供大规模III期RCT所需的因果效力数据。\",\n  \"decision\": \"external_research\",\n  \"still_missing\": \"需要确认是否存在已注册或完成的、专门针对微生物组干预联合ICI治疗实体瘤的III期RCT及其发表的主要疗效结果。当前材料仅证实了此类大型III期RCT在截至2025年的文献中不存在，但未涵盖此后可能完成的新试验。\",\n  \"read_focus\": \"\",\n  \"external_ask\": \"检索ClinicalTrials.gov、WHO ICTRP以及最新发表的医学文献，查找自2025年以来是否有任何完成的、大规模的III期随机对照试验评估FMT、益生菌或定义明确的菌群联合体与ICI联合用于实体瘤患者，并报告OS、PFS或ORR等主要疗效终点。\",\n  \"reason\": \"问题要求识别“已完成的”大规模III期RCT。提供的材料（包括2026年的综述和2024/2025年的原始研究）一致表明，截至其发表时，此类III期RCT尚未完成或发表。综述明确陈述“no completed Phase III randomized trials have yet confirmed...”，而原始研究均为I期或II期单臂试验。因此，基于当前材料可以确认在该时间点之前没有此类研究，但为了回答“是否有”这一存在性问题，特别是考虑到临床研究的滞后性和新试验的可能完成，需要外部检索以确认是否有更新的材料填补了这一空白，或者确认该缺口持续存在。由于核心成功标准是识别具体的III期RCT结果，而现有材料仅提供早期阶段数据和关于缺失的声明，故判定为external_research。\"\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n    - **Gap ID:** Nb6cbac1884a1\n    - **Intended Use:** mechanism\n    - **Local Search:** Found true, 6 papers seen.\n    - **Material Found:** 5 items (mostly summaries/abstracts/fulltexts of specific studies/reviews).\n        - Item 1: Review (2026) on engineering microbial metabolites. Explicitly states *no completed Phase III RCTs* exist as of late 2025. Details ongoing Phase I/Ib trials (FMT, SER-401, SYNB1891, MRx0518), mechanistic rationales (SCFAs, tryptophan derivatives, bile acids), and regulatory/safety challenges.\n        - Item 2 & 3: Abstract CT258 (2024) - Phase II trial (FMT-LUMINate) of FMT + dual ICI in advanced melanoma (n=20). Reports safety, ORR 70%, microbiome shifts, avatar mouse validation. Not Phase III.\n        - Item 4 & 5: Fulltext/Summary (2025) - MIMic phase I trial (oral FMT + anti-PD1 in advanced melanoma, n=20). Reports safety, ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 mo, mOS 52.8 mo. Compares to historical RCTs but explicitly notes no control arm, small sample, hypothesis-generating. Mentions planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17). Not Phase III.\n    - **Paper Context:** Provides titles, years, and some extracted text matching the materials above. Confirms the nature of the studies (Phase I/II, reviews, abstracts).\n    - **Question:** \"Are there any completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials of microbiome interventions (FMT, probiotics, defined consortia) in ICI-treated solid tumour patients reporting primary efficacy outcomes (OS/PFS/ORR)?\"\n    - **Reading Mode:** initial_read\n    - **Success Criteria:** Identify any registered/completed Phase III RCTs or confirm their absence through registry searches/systematic review cross-referencing.\n    - **User Scope:** How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? (Note: The question is specifically